After sending countless cavemen to their doom, Gub became my first 3.4.1
ascension. A large chunk of the credit for this has to be given to his
finding a wand of wishing early in the game, which gave him powered-up
GDSM. Amazing what a difference that makes, particularly in the mines;
don't have to worry about polymorph traps anymore. Tiamat almost got him,
if I remember correctly, as did a gargoyle on the Medusa level, but some
potions of full healing helped save the day. Along with the WoW, he found a
ring of regeneration early on which proved to be a great help. I didn't do
much sacrificing, because I don't know of any weapon better for a Caveman
than The Sceptre of Might.

Used the two scrolls of genocide he found to get rid of the two mind-flayer
varieties.

The game was kind of stingy with armor, which is why he ended up wearing an
elven cloak the whole way.

Killed all the "normal" demon lords except Asmodeus, who was content to
take a 10-zorkmid bribe and leave. Yeenoghu turned up, but no Demogorgon. I
was surprised to learn that Orcustown can turn up *after* you've reached
the Wizard's level. (For the first time, on the "outside.")

Unlike some previous attempts, Gub found several magic markers and had lots
of blank scrolls, so he charged up his armor before taking the final
plunge. The improved AC helped a lot, and he did much better than the two
or three Cavemen before him that got picked off post-Wizard. Had more
trouble with Moloch's arch-priest than with Rodney. Didn't even get
double-teamed, although he did steal the Amulet on the plane of earth; I
appreciate the DevTeam throwing us players a bone and not letting us portal
off the level without the Amulet; I didn't realize it was gone, and had to
go back hunting for it.

Beside the armor, wished for a ring of levitation after Gub got trapped on
the wrong side of the Castle trap doors, thanks to a pit or something. Also
got a t-shirt to fill out the armor, and a freed genie gave a pair of
dexterity gloves which never got used. Got sick of fruitless searching for
the portal on the plane of air, and burned one last wish on a crystal ball.
(The Sceptre's invoked power was a great help there; it was sorta weird
wandering around the place after the monsters had all killed each other...)
Used the CB on all the rest of the levels as well; speeded things up
immensely.

On the Astral plane, killed Pestilence in person, while the other two
Riders were, again, cut down by Conflict.They never got near Gub.
The first temple he tried was the right one, in both senses, and off he
went...

Time now to go to work on a spellcaster.


